{"id": "section-body-14355", "title": "Astigmatism", "chapterId": "chapter-fourteen", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "EYE DISEASES AND REFRACTIVE ERRORS", "Major Blinding Eye Diseases", "Astigmatism"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-14355", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Astigmatism", "runs": [{"text": "Astigmatism"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "1312"}}, {"id": "body-14356", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "This is a condition where the cornea and sometimes the lens have different radius of curvature in all meridians (different focus in different planes). Some myopic and hyperopic patients may have astigmatism.", "runs": [{"text": "This"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "condition"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "where"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cornea"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sometimes"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "lens"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "have"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "different"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "radius"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "curvature"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "all"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "meridians"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(different"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "focus in different planes). Some myopic and hyperopic patients may have astigmatism."}]}, {"id": "body-14359", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-14360", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Poor vision at distance", "runs": [{"text": "Poor"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "vision"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "at"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "distance"}], "list": {"level": 4, "numberingId": "1312"}}, {"id": "body-14361", "type": "